Z||000000||rc5star||08-25-2001||09:32 AM||||O.K. first of all Im a rockie at all of this so any help would be VERY appreciated. Thanks.<P>My car was running good but it leaked oil real bad so I replaced the oil pan gasket (that sucked) and the oil pump too. I replaced the head gasket and all the other gaskets that had to be removed along the way. While I was at it I put in new: distributar, accel coil, spark plugs & wires, thermostate, belts, rockers and rods.<P>The problem: <P>After I put it all back together it wont start. It turns over but it wont catch. Any ideas????<P>I tried to follow the manuals as best as I could but I might of missed something. Any ideas would be great. Thanks.||||reg||8
Z||000001||Joe Torma||08-25-2001||10:35 AM||||Well, I first would check for spark and gas.<P>You hear the fuel pump run right?  <P>A common problem when you take everything apart, is not having the distributor where its supposed to be.  Check your wires.<P>Let us know how you put everything back together.<P><BR>||||reg||1
